   "titulo": "From the educated to the plane",
   "texto": [
    "The flat-shaped verbs are those in the dictionary: **いく** (go), **たべる** (eat). Denial ends in **ない**: **いかない** (not going), **たべない** (not eating). The past ends in **た**: **いった** (I went), **たべた** (I ate).",
    "For «go» and «eat» in the educated form, instead, you have **いきます** and **たべます**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The adjectives and the verb be",
   "texto": [
    "**です** becomes **だ**: **これ は ほん だ** (this is a book). The denial is **じゃない** (it is not), and the past is **だった**.",
    "The adjectives in -i do not change much: **さむい** (it is cold) → **さむかった** (it was cold)."
   ]
